      "name": "blocked-build-dependencies",
      "title": "Blocked build dependencies — read the refusal before you work around it",
      "description": "A build or a model download fails from an agent container. Read which of three different refusals it is before doing anything — a policy denial (403 on CONNECT), an upstream rate limit (429), or a host that is simply down — because each has a different remedy. Covers the Maven Central mirror that gets a Gradle or Maven build through a 429, which hosts were measured open and shut, and when the work belongs to an agent with different network access instead.",
